   "user_head": "TASK\nBring the red chair closer to the brown table. Leave its orientation unchanged.\n\nYou are editing a rigid-body indoor scene. No images are attached; identify objects from the labels and colors in the scene JSON.\n\nSCENE CONVENTIONS\n- Units are meters, kilograms and seconds in a right-handed, Z-up world frame. The floor top surface is at z = 0.\n- quaternion_wxyz is an active rotation from the object's local frame to the world frame, ordered [w, x, y, z], unit length. A pure yaw of theta radians about +Z is [cos(theta/2), 0, 0, sin(theta/2)]; yawing an object by delta multiplies its current quaternion on the left by that yaw quaternion.\n- geometry.aabb_local_min/max is the object's bounding box in its own frame (it rotates with the object). geometry.aabb_world_min/max is the same box in world coordinates at the CURRENT pose; recompute it yourself if you rotate the object.\n- geometry.support_anchor_local is the lowest point of the object in its local frame. An unrotated (or yaw-only rotated) object resting on a horizontal support of height h has position z = h - support_anchor_local[2]. Objects with different heights therefore need different z values at the same support.\n- geometry"
